WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:06.055
Bobby was glad to be outside for the start of cooking class.

2
00:00:06.056 --> 00:00:10.586
The kids were picking tomatoes to make tomato and pasta soup.

3
00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:13.462
Bobby picked a plump tomato.

4
00:00:13.463 --> 00:00:16.602
It felt warm in his hand.

5
00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:19.908
He picked two more.

6
00:00:19.909 --> 00:00:22.775
That gave him an idea.

7
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:25.993
"Hey, want to see me juggle?"

8
00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:29.266
His friends watched him.

9
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:34.876
Bobby tossed the tomatoes in the air.

10
00:00:34.877 --> 00:00:37.803
He caught one but dropped two.

11
00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.811
Jason handed Bobby another tomato.

12
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:45.961
"Here, try it with just two."

13
00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:49.547
Bobby juggled the two tomatoes without dropping them.

14
00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.930
"That's pretty good," Nina said.

15
00:00:52.931 --> 00:00:55.915
Jason handed Bobby one more tomato.

16
00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:59.290
"Now try three at a time."

17
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:03.782
"Ugh!" Bobby dropped two.

18
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:06.486
"It’s harder than it looks!"

19
00:01:06.487 --> 00:01:12.588
He glanced at the tomatoes on the ground. "Uh-oh."

20
00:01:12.589 --> 00:01:16.018
"What's wrong?" Izzie asked.

21
00:01:16.019 --> 00:01:18.901
Bobby picked up a tomato.

22
00:01:18.902 --> 00:01:22.503
"Look, it’s all squishy."

23
00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:25.761
The other tomatoes were bruised too.

24
00:01:25.762 --> 00:01:30.659
Nina gulped. "Chef will be mad.

25
00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.932
He doesn't like to waste food."

26
00:01:33.933 --> 00:01:39.510
"I hope we don't ruin the tomato and pasta soup," Izzie said.

27
00:01:39.511 --> 00:01:43.221
"Maybe he won't notice," Bobby said.

28
00:01:43.222 --> 00:01:47.330
"Let's put the bruised tomatoes on the bottom of the basket.

29
00:01:47.331 --> 00:01:51.600
We'll put good ones on top."

30
00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:55.384
The kids carried the baskets inside.

31
00:01:55.385 --> 00:01:59.251
"Such beautiful tomatoes!" Chef said.

32
00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:02.345
"Our soup will be delicious."

33
00:02:02.346 --> 00:02:05.728
The kids exchanged nervous looks.

34
00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:14.245
"Let's start cooking," Chef said.

35
00:02:14.246 --> 00:02:16.956
"First we'll dice one tomato.

36
00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:20.253
We'll cut the rest of them into quarters."

37
00:02:20.254 --> 00:02:22.742
The kids began cutting.

38
00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:26.609
Soon the good tomatoes were cut up.

39
00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:31.159
Chef picked up a bruised tomato. "What happened?

40
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.788
Here’s another bruised one! And another!"

41
00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:41.765
"I—It's . . . my fault," Bobby said.

42
00:02:41.766 --> 00:02:47.635
"I tried juggling them, and dropped a bunch. I'm sorry."

43
00:02:47.636 --> 00:02:51.033
Chef frowned.

44
00:02:51.034 --> 00:02:56.666
"Should I throw the bad tomatoes in the compost bin?" Bobby asked.

45
00:02:56.667 --> 00:03:02.046
"Of course not!" Chef said.

46
00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.898
"We're not wasting these tomatoes.

47
00:03:04.899 --> 00:03:08.921
And bruised ones are fine in this soup."

48
00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.312
"Phew!" Bobby said.

49
00:03:12.313 --> 00:03:19.750
"Just don't juggle vegetables or fruit again during class," Chef said.

50
00:03:19.751 --> 00:03:23.680
They finished cutting up all the tomatoes.

51
00:03:23.681 --> 00:03:29.071
"Now we have to puree the quartered tomatoes," Izzie said.

52
00:03:29.072 --> 00:03:32.805
They put the tomatoes into a blender.

53
00:03:32.806 --> 00:03:38.862
Whirr! Soon the tomatoes were a smooth puree.

54
00:03:38.863 --> 00:03:44.675
Bobby grinned. "No more bruised tomatoes!"

55
00:03:44.676 --> 00:03:49.193
Izzie chopped green onions while Bobby chopped garlic.

56
00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:52.732
Nina added olive oil to a large pot.

57
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:57.352
Jason cooked the green onions and garlic in the oil.

58
00:03:57.353 --> 00:04:00.412
Then Chef gave Bobby a mesh strainer.

59
00:04:00.413 --> 00:04:03.251
"Hold this over the pot."

60
00:04:03.252 --> 00:04:08.002
Bobby held the strainer while Chef poured the pureed tomatoes through it.

61
00:04:08.003 --> 00:04:16.490
Next they added the diced tomato, heavy cream, water, salt, and black pepper.

62
00:04:16.491 --> 00:04:20.398
"Now we add the pasta," Izzie said.

63
00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:25.670
Chef nodded. "It makes the soup rich and filling.

64
00:04:25.671 --> 00:04:30.756
You can use any short pasta like farfalle or macaroni."

65
00:04:30.757 --> 00:04:38.439
"I like farfalle. That pasta looks like bowties!" Jason said.

66
00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.767
Soon a wonderful aroma filled the air.

67
00:04:42.768 --> 00:04:46.765
Ding! The timer went off.

68
00:04:46.766 --> 00:04:51.214
"The soup's ready!" Nina said.

69
00:04:51.215 --> 00:04:54.388
Chef passed out steaming bowls of soup.

70
00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.593
He sprinkled fresh basil leaves on top.

71
00:04:58.594 --> 00:05:01.289
Bobby tasted the soup.

72
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.519
It was warm and delicious.

73
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.733
Chef looked at Bobby.

74
00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:09.703
"I hope you learned something today."

75
00:05:09.704 --> 00:05:18.070
Bobby nodded. "I sure did. Tomatoes aren't balls!"

